   {
    "id": "h4_00017",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     39
    ],
    "text": "[A51][/A51]APPLICATION USAGE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A51": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_130_07\" id=\"tag_17_130_07\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00018",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     41,
     1
    ],
    "text": "When a stream that has unwritten buffered data is flushed by [I52]exit[/I52]() there is no way for the calling process to discover\nwhether or not [I53]exit[/I53]() successfully wrote the data to the underlying file descriptor. Therefore, it is strongly recommended\nthat applications always ensure there is no unwritten buffered data in any stream when calling [I54]exit[/I54](), or returning from the\ninitial call to [I55]main[/I55](), with a [I56]status[/I56] value that indicates no errors occurred.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I52": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I53": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I54": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I55": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I56": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00019",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     41,
     3
    ],
    "text": "For example, the following code demonstrates one way to ensure that [I57]stdout[/I57] has already been successfully flushed before\ncalling [I58]exit[/I58]() with status 0. If the flush fails, the file descriptor underlying [I59]stdout[/I59] is closed so that\n[I60]exit[/I60]() will not try to repeat the failed write operation. If the flush succeeds, a final check with [A61][I62]ferror[/I62]()[/A61] is performed to ensure that there were no write errors during earlier flush\noperations (that were not handled at the time).",
    "placeholders": {
     "I57": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I58": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I59": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I60": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A61": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/ferror.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I62": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
